EXT. HARBOR PARKING LOT - FOOD TRUCK "THE GOLDEN GOBLIN" - DAY

A rusty purple truck with a huge cartoon goblin painted on the side. Its painted eyes blink when nobody's looking. A line of hungry customers stretches around the block.

Inside the truck, a tiny kitchen. Steam, sizzle, clatter.

BIG DAVE, 50s, an enormous man with an apron that reads "Kiss the Cook (Please)," flips a patty. Beside him, MO, 20s, wiry, chops onions with a nervous speed. At the window, JEN, 30s, sharp ponytail, takes orders with a grin that could cut glass.

Perched on the shelf above the fryer sits SAM, a one-foot-tall goblin in a chef's hat, grumpy, covered in flour. Only the crew can see him.

JEN
(to the line)
Next! What'll it be?

BIG DAVE
(to the whole kitchen)
Orders up, people! Let's move!

MO
(to himself, muttering)
Don't cut your finger. Don't cut your finger.

SAM
(dry)
Mo, you've said that eleven times. I'm counting.

MO
(not looking up)
You're not helping, Sam.

JEN
(over her shoulder)
Two Goblin Specials and a side of fries!

BIG DAVE
(flipping)
Fries are in the basket, Mo!

MO
(to himself)
I know. I know where the fries are.

Jen's phone RINGS on the counter. She answers on speaker.

MRS. K (V.O.)
(over the phone, crackling)
Jennifer? It is Mrs. K. I am watching the line on the news. It is too long.

JEN
(through gritted teeth)
Mrs. K, we're doing great. Lots of customers.

MRS. K (V.O.)
Too many customers is no profit if you give them free pickles.

BIG DAVE
(quietly)
Who told her about the pickles?

SAM
(shrugging)
She has her ways.

MRS. K (V.O.)
I hear everything. Mo is cutting too slow.

MO
(freezing)
I'm not cutting too slow!

MRS. K (V.O.)
Mo, speak to me when your onions are finished.

Mo glances at Big Dave. Big Dave shakes his head slowly.

JEN
(to the group)
Okay, everyone calm down.

NOBODY CALMS DOWN. The fryer HISSES. Smoke curls toward the ceiling.

SAM
(standing on the shelf, alarmed)
Dave, the oil's too hot.

BIG DAVE
(waving it off)
It's fine.

SAM
Dave.

BIG DAVE
It's fine!

The fryer POPS. A tiny fireball rolls up the wall.

MO
(shrieking)
FIRE!

JEN
(to the phone)
Mrs. K, I'll call you back!

MRS. K (V.O.)
Jennifer, do not hang up on--

Jen hangs up. Big Dave grabs a fire extinguisher. SPLOOSH. A cloud of white foam engulfs the kitchen.

Silence. Everyone is covered in foam. Sam wipes his face with one tiny hand.

SAM
(deadpan)
I told you.

From outside, the line of customers CHEERS.
